{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits","id":1006919,"title":"Sphere Limits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T17:31:45-08:00","id":1006919,"title":"Sphere Limits","content":"I have a question for the hive mind. What is the consensus on the limits of mages spheres?<br /> <br /> Should a mage be able to do anything so long as they have enough successes and the right spheres or should mages have things that they just can't do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T17:36:53-08:00","id":1006921,"title":"","content":"Personally I subscribe to the &quot;What can be made by magic can be broken or changed by magic.&quot; view. And since everything is made by magic....<br /> <br /> Others don't and M20 includes earthly foundations which are stupid and ill defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T17:47:19-08:00","id":1006928,"title":"","content":"Paradigm above all else. If the mage doesn't believe something is possible, or thinks that something is specifically impossible, then no amount of extra sphere juice is going to undo how they think about it.<br /> <br /> For example, I once played an Etherite while another guy played something else (I forget). We both had Entropy 1 and were looking for some sacred tablets which were hidden in a warehouse.<br /> He did an Entropy 1 effect in order to look for things with a great amount of &quot;importance&quot;. I wanted to do the same kind of effect, but I couldn't because it didn't make any sense to my guy, in his mind &quot;importance&quot; isn't something which can be quantified, so the effect just wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:31:24-08:00","id":1007079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits#post1006919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question for the hive mind. What is the consensus on the limits of mages spheres?<br /> <br /> Should a mage be able to do anything so long as they have enough successes and the right spheres or should mages have things that they just can't do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some things are \u201ctechnically\u201c impossible (like creating a Tellurian/Reality/Realm that is not based on quintessence).<br /> Otherwise I would say hard limits are on things the troupe doesn't want to be possible (some don't like sacrifices for quint).<br /> The other things are possible, at least in theory.<br /> If something demands multiple masterlevel spheres and 248 successes, then it is not very likely to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:50:58-08:00","id":1007356,"title":"","content":"Like Saikou, Paradigm above anything else. I have a player in the game I'm running who plays a Cultist half-niki minaj, half-miley Cirus, half-Sia (yes, it's three halves...). Well... obviously she will not be a fireball caster kind of Mage ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:12:24-08:00","id":1007365,"title":"","content":"You should have qualified it by saying &quot;Importance to me.&quot; That would have clarified things a little bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T20:50:13-08:00","id":1007542,"title":"","content":"The tone and themes of your chronicle should also influence what is possible or how easy it is to achieve. Time travel that doesn't involve absurd degrees of risk is a great way to rob a story of its weight. Don't plan on having a &quot;who's the secret Nephandi&quot; plot if you allow some combination of Mind/Time/Spirit/Prime/Entropy to sense evil. Right now I'm running a pulp WW2 game where a character made a bunch of APCs able to burrow through the earth. In a modern, gritty game about escaping the NWO, should that be possible? Technically yes, but as an ST I'd ask players to stick to ideas not featured in Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T00:41:37-08:00","id":1007606,"title":"","content":"Also, it is stated quite clearly in most of the books. Especially when rotes are described. It is clear that those rotes are paradigm dependent. That does not mean that the effects are not possible in other paradigms that the one described by the practice of a specific rote. However, it does imply that a specific rote is linked to a specific practice. Moreover, several rotes have drawbacks or limitations (some spell only applies on women, some other needs you to cut of your arm or eat a living heart,...). Mage: the Ascension (as opposed to the Awakening) falls within the post-modern philosophy which emphasizes the personalization and the subjective construction of reality. Postmodern philosophers deny that an objective reality exist. This is the core of the game, so putting it aside is misunderstanding the game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That was to clarify my point: Something being game-mechanically possible should not necessary being feasible by any Mage since his practice depends on his own specific belief and paradigm.<br /> <br /> That said, if your Mage can find a way to fold a specific effect in his paradigm, it's okay of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 11-24-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T08:45:27-08:00","id":1007721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1007079#post1007079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some things are \u201ctechnically\u201c impossible (like creating a Tellurian/Reality/Realm that is not based on quintessence).<br /> Otherwise I would say hard limits are on things the troupe doesn't want to be possible (some don't like sacrifices for quint).<br /> The other things are possible, at least in theory.<br /> If something demands multiple masterlevel spheres and 248 successes, then it is not very likely to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.... With the Arch-Mastery of Prime you can do that. Create a new universe that doesn't require quintessence from this one to support it I mean.<br /> <br /> Though everything from that universe will disintigrate if taken into our universe, due to the higher energy level from ours. This is why I think that setting wise, it makes the most sense if &quot;God&quot; was actually an insanely OP mage from another universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T10:41:34-08:00","id":1007761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1007721#post1007721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh.... With the Arch-Mastery of Prime you can do that. Create a new universe that doesn't require quintessence from this one to support it I mean.<br /> <br /> Though everything from that universe will disintigrate if taken into our universe, due to the higher energy level from ours. This is why I think that setting wise, it makes the most sense if &amp;quot;God&amp;quot; was actually an insanely OP mage from another universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what is the base component of the created universe? I didn't mean that you have to use quintessence, but your effect is composed of quint. You could not possibly work otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T11:27:25-08:00","id":1007780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1007761#post1007761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what is the base component of the created universe? I didn't mean that you have to use quintessence, but your effect is composed of quint. You could not possibly work otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOOOOH.<br /> <br /> Ok. I was thinking you were talking about Horizon realms and how they're tied to nodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:32:00-08:00","id":1008143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1006928#post1006928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradigm above all else. If the mage doesn't believe something is possible, or thinks that something is specifically impossible, then no amount of extra sphere juice is going to undo how they think about it.<br /> <br /> For example, I once played an Etherite while another guy played something else (I forget). We both had Entropy 1 and were looking for some sacred tablets which were hidden in a warehouse.<br /> He did an Entropy 1 effect in order to look for things with a great amount of &quot;importance&quot;. I wanted to do the same kind of effect, but I couldn't because it didn't make any sense to my guy, in his mind &quot;importance&quot; isn't something which can be quantified, so the effect just wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember a similar scene from waaaaay back in an early Mage game, where the Hermetic was doing his damnedest to figure out the meaning of a magical sigil using all of his magical knowledge, relevant detection spells (low levels of Prime, Prime and Spirit, etc.). He wasn't getting much in the way of success. The Cultist got bored, used Spirit to awaken the sigil, made friends with it and asked it what it meant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 11-25-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:57:43-08:00","id":1009058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1006921#post1006921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I subscribe to the &quot;What can be made by magic can be broken or changed by magic.&quot; view. And since everything is made by magic....<br /> <br /> Others don't and M20 includes earthly foundations which are stupid and ill defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earthly Foundations (and Reality Zones in general) have nothing to do with what magick can and can't do; they're entirely about what is and isn't <i>Vulgar</i>. \u201cVulgar\u201d is still <i>possible</i>; it's just that you pay a price for it. <br /> <br /> Getting back to the original question of whether or not there things that magick can't do, I'd say that if such things exist at all, they're few and far between; and even then, \u201cmagick can't do this\u201d tends to come with the caveat of \u201c\u2026unless you're an archmage\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:22:43-08:00","id":1009129,"title":"","content":"Frankly though, I think I'm more interesting question would be what must magic do? Is there anything that isn't Magic, and if so where do you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:14:47-08:00","id":1009181,"title":"","content":"I'd say that what is part of the consensus is not Magick. I mean... Take the GPS for exemple. Obviously a correspondance 2 rote but it clearly became mundane when some sleeper dismounted it and mounted it back and it still functioned. At that point, I'd would say that the GPS is not Magick anymore because part of the global consensus.<br /> <br /> This is a way to explain the ascension war and for some Mages, the Ascension itself. Making something wonderful become part of the Consensus defined by mankind. Don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:00:30-08:00","id":1009355,"title":"","content":"Sure GPS is magic. So are toasters. Matter 2: Bread to cooked bread. It's an Instrument with a specific Procedure hardwired in. They even have the possible Paradox Flaws down to a static binomial opposition. &quot;Fail&quot; at your &quot;toaster roll&quot; and you get burned toast or under-done toast. Hells, FIRE is pretty much the same thing. It's an Instrument that can do a lot of Forces 2 and Matter 2 effects (maybe some Mind 2 as well.... so, so cozy.... or, alternatively, VERY scary).<br /> <br /> Magic is everywhere and always. Once it &quot;enters&quot; the Consensus, it becomes static which means the effects of success and failure are defined, but it's still Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T09:18:34-08:00","id":1009361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009355#post1009355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure GPS is magic. So are toasters. Matter 2: Bread to cooked bread. It's an Instrument with a specific Procedure hardwired in. They even have the possible Paradox Flaws down to a static binomial opposition. &quot;Fail&quot; at your &quot;toaster roll&quot; and you get burned toast or under-done toast. Hells, FIRE is pretty much the same thing. It's an Instrument that can do a lot of Forces 2 and Matter 2 effects (maybe some Mind 2 as well.... so, so cozy.... or, alternatively, VERY scary).<br /> <br /> Magic is everywhere and always. Once it &quot;enters&quot; the Consensus, it becomes static which means the effects of success and failure are defined, but it's still Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was traveling to a new place a Correspondence 3 Rote/Procedure once upon a time? :&gt;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:02:19-08:00","id":1009381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009361#post1009361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was traveling to a new place a Correspondence 3 Rote/Procedure once upon a time? :&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Much fun reading that \u02c6\u02c6<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009355#post1009355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure GPS is magic. So are toasters. Matter 2: Bread to cooked bread. It's an Instrument with a specific Procedure hardwired in. They even have the possible Paradox Flaws down to a static binomial opposition. &quot;Fail&quot; at your &quot;toaster roll&quot; and you get burned toast or under-done toast. Hells, FIRE is pretty much the same thing. It's an Instrument that can do a lot of Forces 2 and Matter 2 effects (maybe some Mind 2 as well.... so, so cozy.... or, alternatively, VERY scary).<br /> <br /> Magic is everywhere and always. Once it &quot;enters&quot; the Consensus, it becomes static which means the effects of success and failure are defined, but it's still Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree. The WoD is great place where strange things happen and wierder things exist. But it does not mean that everything is magick. True magick is concious and unawakened beings cannot perform True Magick. Since Sleepers can actually achieve some things (well... it can be seducing but no, not everything is discovered by Mages, even if they really want it to be the case, and even if they try to say it to others and to themselves...), these thing are not magick by definition. Then, it exists a time when something magickal suddenly is not anymore. Making reality the way you want it to be is at the core of the Ascension war, don't you think ? The outcome of the Ascension War does not only define what is Vulgar or what is Coincidental. It defines what is part of Reality and what is not. At least, that's my way to describe it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:21:55-08:00","id":1009384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009381#post1009381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Much fun reading that \u02c6\u02c6<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do not agree. The WoD is great place where strange things happen and wierder things exist. But it does not mean that everything is magick. True magick is concious and unawakened beings cannot perform True Magick. Since Sleepers can actually achieve some things (well... it can be seducing but no, not everything is discovered by Mages, even if they really want it to be the case, and even if they try to say it to others and to themselves...), these thing are not magick by definition. Then, it exists a time when something magickal suddenly is not anymore. Making reality the way you want it to be is at the core of the Ascension war, don't you think ? The outcome of the Ascension War does not only define what is Vulgar or what is Coincidental. It defines what is part of Reality and what is not. At least, that's my way to describe it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making toast is conscious. So is making fire. So is making a convincing argument.<br /> <br /> So is walking from one place to another, but, since beings that aren't sentient (meaning also, their spirits aren't Awakened) can do that, like say, &quot;eating&quot; it probably falls under the &quot;not magic&quot; side of things. That's &quot;the way the world works&quot;. Once you gain sentient you are able change things.<br /> <br /> Your test for magic isn't what you're saying it is. You want magic to be BREAKING the rules. But it's not. If it was, then ALL Magic would be Vulgar. It's not. You can consciously modify reality without breaking it. That's what coincidental magic is. That's why it's easier (which, is from a game design perspective ass-backwards, but... whatever. In Mage, as in all White Wolf, What is is what has been and ever shall be, bad design notwithstanding). And conscious beings who are not Awakened can manipulate reality. Static mages can do it by application of will to cause a change in reality that is, effectively, bending, cracking or breaking it, just not with the insane flexibility of an Awakened mage, but conscious beings who cannot do static or dynamic mages can still change reality, they're just restricted in the ways in which they can do so. Effectively, it has to be entirely coincidental and fall along long predetermined lines as to what cause generates what effect.<br /> <br /> You want magic to be special. And in Mage, it's just not. It's everything. A car is magic. A toaster. Rhianna. A vampire. The Dark Umbra. Albuquerque. The Moon. Tomorrow. Napoleon. Gerbils. What makes mages special is that they know how to get around the boring stuff and exploit the cracks to make things that could potentially happen, happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:50:14-08:00","id":1009393,"title":"","content":"OK, as many times, we disagree at almost every level ^^<br /> <br /> I do not want Magick to be special. I just say that everything is not Magick. Choices can change events and theories can influence the consensus. This is entirely different from cutting off a pattern of the tapestry to replace it by a pattern of your own making which describes true Magick. You accord too much to Mages. Mages are people before being Awakened beings. They are just the ones that had their belief so strong it enables them to actually rape reality to make it their bitch. Far from what Sleepers can do. Of course people can do things. That is the reason why the Consensus is still something changing. But if everything was Magick, then what would be the point of convincing sleepers that another way is possible. You would just have to show them directly your way in the most vulgar way. What I mean is that the sole Magick of sleepers is actually the power to shift the consensus. Mages can only influence it indirectly by influencing the sleepers.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, it seems to me that we disagree on terms. What can be explained with science can also be explained with religion, mysticism, etc. In that way, I'm with you : everything is &quot;magick&quot;. Now, what I call Magick is what is actually not acceptable by the consensus. Our misunderstanding seems to be mainly on definitions. However, what I define as Magick (as not part of the consensus) is not necessary vulgar. Because there is also a difference between Reality and Consensus. Reality is much bigger and that is why True Magick can exist outside the consensus, not because everything is Magick (in the way I define it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:02:38-08:00","id":1009441,"title":"","content":"Magick requires an Avatar. The Avatar doesn't have to be Awake \u2014 the Consensus consists primarily of Sleeping Avatars \u2014 but the Avatar has to be there: dogs, cats, ghosts, and spirits don't have Avatars, and so don't do magick. <br /> <br /> Also, not everything that's supernatural requires magick: see the aforementioned ghosts and spirits, and add vampires, werewolves, and the like. No Avatar, no magick; but still supernatural.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:11:33-08:00","id":1009449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009393#post1009393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, as many times, we disagree at almost every level ^^<br /> <br /> I do not want Magick to be special. I just say that everything is not Magick. Choices can change events and theories can influence the consensus. This is entirely different from cutting off a pattern of the tapestry to replace it by a pattern of your own making which describes true Magick. You accord too much to Mages. Mages are people before being Awakened beings. They are just the ones that had their belief so strong it enables them to actually rape reality to make it their bitch. Far from what Sleepers can do. Of course people can do things. That is the reason why the Consensus is still something changing. But if everything was Magick, then what would be the point of convincing sleepers that another way is possible. You would just have to show them directly your way in the most vulgar way. What I mean is that the sole Magick of sleepers is actually the power to shift the consensus. Mages can only influence it indirectly by influencing the sleepers.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, it seems to me that we disagree on terms. What can be explained with science can also be explained with religion, mysticism, etc. In that way, I'm with you : everything is &quot;magick&quot;. Now, what I call Magick is what is actually not acceptable by the consensus. Our misunderstanding seems to be mainly on definitions. However, what I define as Magick (as not part of the consensus) is not necessary vulgar. Because there is also a difference between Reality and Consensus. Reality is much bigger and that is why True Magick can exist outside the consensus, not because everything is Magick (in the way I define it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That's what I said. For you, magic(k) is breaking things. (I.e. Mages are less exalted beings reweaving reality in accord to higher sensibilities than they are raging spoiled toddlers who scream about what they WANT, WANT, WANT, until reality gives way, just to shut them up, or doesn't, and they end up being punished for their behavior, a.k.a Paradox...) <br /> <br /> But that's not magic(k) in the game. Or else coincidental magic wouldn't be a thing in the game. And it most certainly wouldn't be rewarded. Convincing the Consensus wouldn't matter because the Consensus doesn't matter. If only the special snowflakes are the realities darlings, then mass belief wouldn't matter a fig. But, it's the &quot;way things work&quot; as understood by just plain EVERYONE that matters much, much, much more than what mages do. <br /> <br /> It's like the magic of the world is a glacier...a giant settled coherent mass. Static magic is the places where conditions are just so that liquid water can run, trickle and collect, before inevitably re-freezing. True magic is amazingly rare, like the triple point conditions where the water can be either in any form, liquid, gas or solid. But it's all just water/magic(k)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:22:36-08:00","id":1009455,"title":"","content":"Yep. Although, the nature of Avatars might not be that simple. Avatars are not &quot;there&quot; waiting for the Sleeper to Awake. They're far away spirits matched to the Sleeper when said sleeper awakens, fated to guide the newly Mage towards enlightment : &quot;An Avatar first comes to a mage in the moment of Epiphany, at the point where mortal illusions disappear.&quot; (M20, p.44) There are several mentions of the spiritual entities (Psychopomps) that guide the Avatar to the Mage. You can find references in the first edition of Mage: The Ascension, also in Infinite Tapestry and Time of Judgment: Ascension (which gives a whole End of Times scenario concerning the Anakim, the willing Mage possessed by such a Psychopomp). Oddly, there is no direct mention of Psychopomps in the M20 corebook.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that the nature presence of the Avatar is subject to discussion, especially between Mages of different Traditions (even inside Traditions...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:08:50-08:00","id":1009474,"title":"","content":"That is more M20 sillyness. That makes both the existence of widderslainte and the Progenitors campaign to eliminate sleepers Avatars nonsensical.<br /> <br /> The setting all but outright states your avatar is with you from birth until death. (And possibly beyond if you're a Lich.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:47:01-08:00","id":1009487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009474#post1009474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is more M20 sillyness. That makes both the existence of widderslainte and the Progenitors campaign to eliminate sleepers Avatars nonsensical.<br /> <br /> The setting all but outright states your avatar is with you from birth until death. (And possibly beyond if you're a Lich.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not an M20 sillyness. As I said, it is not mentioned in M20. It's from previous settings and editions. But it can ben put aside (as I do as a matter of fact ^^)<br /> <br /> Where did you read that it was with the Mage from birth please ? I cannot find the source. Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 11-28-2016, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:10:15-08:00","id":1009553,"title":"","content":"There's a bit in the Progenitor convention book about trying to eliminate the masses Avatars, and also generate a means to induce an avatar in those who don't have one. Which, if they actually got it to work, would cripple the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Two the Widderslaintes, who are only different from normal people on account of inheriting an inverted avatar, are bad from birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:12:09-08:00","id":1009554,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's MRev silliness. I don't recall seeing it before or since.<br /> <br /> When and how someone gets an avatar is an open question. What's known is it most everybody has one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:15:27-08:00","id":1009673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009455#post1009455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Although, the nature of Avatars might not be that simple. Avatars are not &quot;there&quot; waiting for the Sleeper to Awake. They're far away spirits matched to the Sleeper when said sleeper awakens, fated to guide the newly Mage towards enlightment : &quot;An Avatar first comes to a mage in the moment of Epiphany, at the point where mortal illusions disappear.&quot; (M20, p.44) (...)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009474#post1009474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is more M20 sillyness. That makes both the existence of widderslainte and the Progenitors campaign to eliminate sleepers Avatars nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be reconciled with the existence of Widderslaintes - the Inverted Avatar would attach to them around birth. Then there's the question why aren't they Awakened from birth - though this could be chalked up as the way Widderslaintes function.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Progenitor ambition doesn't make much sense, considering it would also get rid of Genius - unless they think that Avatars are something specific to mystic Mages...But you'd think that a Technocrat who knows enough about Avatars to have the ambition of getting rid of sleeping Avatars, would also be aware that it would hit Technocracy just as hard. Unless the plan is to eliminate Avatars and make do with the Technocrats who are already Enlightened; which would be pretty grim and radical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-29-2016, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T02:16:25-08:00","id":1009695,"title":"","content":"I am not fond of those Psychopomps entities. However, not fond neither about the &quot;Avatar from birth thing&quot;. I find nowhere mention of that. The only thing that is found is that the Avatar is there when the Mage Awakens and guides him/her through the Enlightment process. It is never stated that it is there before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:40:28-08:00","id":1009709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009695#post1009695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, not fond neither about the &quot;Avatar from birth thing&quot;. I find nowhere mention of that. The only thing that is found is that the Avatar is there when the Mage Awakens and guides him/her through the Enlightment process. It is never stated that it is there before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Choir's idea of each human having a fragment of the One in themselves could imply Avatars being in humans from birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-29-2016, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:36:48-08:00","id":1009722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009695#post1009695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not fond of those Psychopomps entities. However, not fond neither about the &quot;Avatar from birth thing&quot;. I find nowhere mention of that. The only thing that is found is that the Avatar is there when the Mage Awakens and guides him/her through the Enlightment process. It is never stated that it is there before.</div> </div> </div> </div> What do you think the Consensus is? It's the cumulative effect of all of the Avatars of Sleepers. In fact, \u201cSleeper\u201d and \u201cAwakened\u201d are references to the state of the Avatar; its presence both before and after the Awakening is never questioned in any edition of the game. Even Revised doesn't say that psychopomps attach the Avatar at the moment of Awakening; they do so long before that, probably at some point when the person is still in the womb. It takes something like Gilgul to get a human without an Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T06:20:52-08:00","id":1009743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009722#post1009722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What do you think the Consensus is? It's the cumulative effect of all of the Avatars of Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wwaowaowaowo This is interpreting as hell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is really diminishing for regular poeple. Poeple are not just empty shells unable to believe nor have convictions. Not everything is due to Avatars. I consider that the Consensus is defined by the human mind alone, actually the sum of everyone's convictions. In my opinion, Avatars have influence only when the Mage awakens. Well, that's my interpretation, feel free to have yours <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009722#post1009722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Revised doesn't say that psychopomps attach the Avatar at the moment of Awakening; they do so long before that, probably at some point when the person is still in the womb. It takes something like Gilgul to get a human without an Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I did not see that way. Why not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:01:39-08:00","id":1009790,"title":"","content":"Are you under the impression that the Avatar is some kind of alien symbiote? If so, let me correct that impression: the Avatar is a manifestation of the person's soul. It becomes part of the person when the person's soul forms. By definition, it's whatever it is about humans that enables their beliefs and will to shape reality. The Avatar cannot shape reality by itself; it has to be directed by the person's beliefs and fueled by the person's will. Far from diminishing humans, the fact that every one of them has an Avatar <i>elevates</i> them. There are plenty of creatures out there that have beliefs and will, from the mundane (animals) to the supernatural (vampires and werewolves, ghosts and goblins); and none of them have any ability to shape reality. Tremere found that out the hard way. Only humans translate their beliefs into change, and the Avatar is what does the translation. No Avatar, no magick.<br /> <br /> In the Consensus, the Avatar is kind of like citizenship: it's that innate quality of the person that allows her beliefs to factor in, for her vote to be counted. It's why spirits don't dominate the Consensus: without Avatars, their beliefs don't count. So yes, the Consensus is the sum of every human's convictions; and Avatars are <i>why</i> this is so. And the only difference between a Sleeping Avatar and one that's Awake is that the latter can <i>consciously, deliberately, and actively</i> shape reality; while the former only shape reality subconsciously and passively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-29-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T12:01:05-08:00","id":1010743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1009790#post1009790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you under the impression that the Avatar is some kind of alien symbiote? If so, let me correct that impression: the Avatar is a manifestation of the person's soul. It becomes part of the person when the person's soul forms. By definition, it's whatever it is about humans that enables their beliefs and will to shape reality. The Avatar cannot shape reality by itself; it has to be directed by the person's beliefs and fueled by the person's will. Far from diminishing humans, the fact that every one of them has an Avatar <i>elevates</i> them. There are plenty of creatures out there that have beliefs and will, from the mundane (animals) to the supernatural (vampires and werewolves, ghosts and goblins); and none of them have any ability to shape reality. Tremere found that out the hard way. Only humans translate their beliefs into change, and the Avatar is what does the translation. No Avatar, no magick.<br /> <br /> In the Consensus, the Avatar is kind of like citizenship: it's that innate quality of the person that allows her beliefs to factor in, for her vote to be counted. It's why spirits don't dominate the Consensus: without Avatars, their beliefs don't count. So yes, the Consensus is the sum of every human's convictions; and Avatars are <i>why</i> this is so. And the only difference between a Sleeping Avatar and one that's Awake is that the latter can <i>consciously, deliberately, and actively</i> shape reality; while the former only shape reality subconsciously and passively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I'm convinced. Now, not totally with Ajax since I do not consider that everything's magick. Magick is the ability to conciously shape reality.<br /> <br /> Concerning the Avatar stuff, I thought about it a lot, and the more I do, the more I'm convinced that the whole Psychopomps thing is not silly at all. Indeed, if the Avatar is there since the birth, it needs to be attached to the human being in the first place. There are multiple references of entities having in charge the whole reincarnation cycle thing, in many religions and cults all other the world. They are the spirits responsible for the journey of the soul from earth to the afterlife, and in religions in which the reincarnation is considered, they bring the soul to the new born.<br /> <br /> You have references in the Christianism where they're refered as angels (Archangel Mickael), in Hindouism with Shiva, ancient Egypt mythology with the god Anubis. You can also name Charon who provides passage to the souls to guide them to hell in greek mythology, or Valkyries in northern mythologies. Psychopomps are merely the help for the soul to travel. They neither judge nor decide what happens to the soul between lives.<br /> <br /> Finding information on the internet about Psychopomps is easy should you search on google. Anyway, I like the idea more and more.<br /> <br /> The only thing I have trouble to imagine is what would be a Psychopomp in a Scientific paradigm. Any ideas ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:48:19-08:00","id":1010797,"title":"","content":"The thing about psychopomps (outside of MRev) is that they're purely theoretical; nobody has ever seen one, and while you can infer their existence, you cannot confirm it. I actually prefer this model, because it allows a wider range of paradigms to be potentially true. <br /> <br /> The difficulty you're running into is that the materialist paradigms don't allow for a soul. As such, most of the Conventions lack an appropriate frame of reference to discuss anything having to do with the Avatar (or, as they call it, Genius). The best they can do is to try to reframe the issue in physical terms (e.g., midichlorians, or alien symbiotes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T21:03:26-08:00","id":1010922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1010743#post1010743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. I'm convinced. Now, not totally with Ajax since I do not consider that everything's magick. Magick is the ability to conciously shape reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That's what I said. But that's not what you are saying. You are still saying magic(k) is the ability to BREAK reality. You are unwilling to allow that there is any other sort of magic than violating the &quot;natural order&quot;. Which is fine, I guess. It's just not this game. Once again. Your definition doesn't work in a game where there is such a thing as Coincidental magic. Coincidental magic is consciously shaping reality. It's also &quot;magic(k)&quot; that fits in with what the Consensus accepts as the way in which consciousness affects reality. Which is what everyone with a consciousness is doing all the time, They just can't do it without all the props and have a more limited set of effects they can cause.<br /> <br /> Once you say &quot;Science/Technology is Magic, Magic is Magic, etc. etc.&quot;, you are allowing for EVERYTHING to be magic. Somehow, I think you are seeing this as somehow demeaning magic in some way. I guess it's because, if magic is everything, everywhere, all the time, it isn't special? But that's just it is. It's the only thing that special, because it's everything that's special. The difference between a Sleeper and an Awakened individual is not that they aren't doing the same things fundamentally, it's that the mage realizes there are less in the way of limitations and that it's actually all full of wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T22:57:27-08:00","id":1010949,"title":"","content":"That is not true. I'm more and more convinced that you mistake coincidental Magick with static Magick. And more generally static Magick and dynamic Magick. Dynamic Magick, what Mages do, is always breaking the rules. Coincidental Magick is just fouling the Consensus while doing it.<br /> <br /> I'll get references later today (now, I'm supposed to be working... ^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:56:06-08:00","id":1011001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1010949#post1010949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not true. I'm more and more convinced that you mistake coincidental Magick with static Magick. And more generally static Magick and dynamic Magick. Dynamic Magick, what Mages do, is always breaking the rules. Coincidental Magick is just fouling the Consensus while doing it.<br /> <br /> I'll get references later today (now, I'm supposed to be working... ^^)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get the reference:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Coincidental Magic<br /> Coincidental</b> magic is the only choice for mages planning on sticking around for any length of time. By couching magical Effects in chance<br /> occurrences, the mage operates in plain sight with potential Sleeper witnesses none the wiser. <u>Such castings are referred to as static magic</u>, as they,<br /> like the powers of the sorcerer, work within the confines of static reality.&quot;<br /> &quot;<b>Vulgar</b> magic, <u>also known as dynamic magic</u>, occurs as the result of a mage forcing reality to conform to his preconceived expectations.&quot;<br /> <br /> So Coincidental magick is Static Magic too. Meanwhile, not all magick Awakened Mages do is Dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:12:22-08:00","id":1011007,"title":"","content":"From where did you get that please ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:42:08-08:00","id":1011013,"title":"","content":"The way I look at it: What sorcerers do? That's in full compliance with the rules. Coincidental Magick? That bends the rules, but doesn't break them. Vulgar Magick breaks the rules. <br /> <br /> There is an important distinction between Hedge Magic and Coincidental Magick: the former doesn't require your Avatar to be Awake, and might not even require you to have an Avatar at all; the latter requires an Awakened Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:53:11-08:00","id":1011017,"title":"","content":"That's what I thought. This is why I have trouble understanding the reference. I think this langage abuse (not sure the expression exists in English...). It states that it behaves the same, but I would have trouble thinking it's the same. For one thing, the Mage does the same thing when he performs coincidental and vulgar Magick. The only difference is the decorum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T05:33:06-08:00","id":1011024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011007#post1011007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From where did you get that please ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corebook, page 137, Chapter 4: The Spheres, section The Ways of Creation / Limits of Awakened Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:46:10-08:00","id":1011049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011024#post1011024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corebook, page 137, Chapter 4: The Spheres, section The Ways of Creation / Limits of Awakened Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 on the other hand clearly states that Static Magic are the rigid powers of Non-mage splats, while Dynamic Magick is what Mages do. And Coincidental Magick is Dynamic Magick hidden under the guise of static reality-conformity.<br /> <br /> (Page 57, &quot;Static Magic, Dynamic Magick, and Technomagick&quot;)<br /> <br /> P.s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;All mages, as noted earlier, work with dynamic magick, even when they don\u2019t define their powers that<br /> way. In the setting, your characters might never understand the difference between a hedge wizard\u2019s spells and the<br /> powers of an Awakened mage. Your players, however, will.</i>&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-02-2016, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:13:18-08:00","id":1011065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011049#post1011049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 on the other hand clearly states that Static Magic are the rigid powers of Non-mage splats, while Dynamic Magick is what Mages do. And Coincidental Magick is Dynamic Magick hidden under the guise of static reality-conformity.<br /> <br /> (Page 57, &quot;Static Magic, Dynamic Magick, and Technomagick&quot;)<br /> <br /> P.s.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought M20 wasn't supposed to make sweeping changes or take rigid stances on the question of which version of the metaphysics is true. Oh well, I sit informed.<br /> <br /> (Hmm. Given that preferences for the editions seem to vary significantly across the fandom, I guess next time I should check whether the OP decides which one is the default assumption for a thread, and if there isn't one, specify which of the canons lists whatever quotes I find in further discussions.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:33:41-08:00","id":1011072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011065#post1011065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I thought M20 wasn't supposed to make sweeping changes or take rigid stances on the question of which version of the metaphysics is true. Oh well, I sit informed.</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, I don't think it has; at least, not in this case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011065#post1011065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Hmm. Given that preferences for the editions seem to vary significantly across the fandom, I guess next time I should check whether the OP decides which one is the default assumption for a thread, and if there isn't one, specify which of the canons lists whatever quotes I find in further discussions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, M20 is taken to be canon on these forums unless specified otherwise. That said, M20 is arguably a \u201cbest of both worlds\u201d synthesis between M2e and MRev, with a slight but noticeable bias toward the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T08:02:34-08:00","id":1011084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011065#post1011065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, I thought M20 wasn't supposed to make sweeping changes or take rigid stances on the question of which version of the metaphysics is true. Oh well, I sit informed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I never really understood the Metaphysics any differently than what M20 states, even in the Revised book era.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the Revised book even describes the 'static effects' of Coincidental Magick as a mere 'mimicry', and the pre-Revised corebooks also state what M20 states...so, in a way, the sweeping change in wording of what the difference between Static and True/Dynamic magic is, was made by Revised <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And in the end didn't make a difference, anyways)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T09:42:30-08:00","id":1011117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1010949#post1010949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not true. I'm more and more convinced that you mistake coincidental Magick with static Magick. And more generally static Magick and dynamic Magick. Dynamic Magick, what Mages do, is always breaking the rules. Coincidental Magick is just fouling the Consensus while doing it.<br /> <br /> I'll get references later today (now, I'm supposed to be working... ^^)</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I don't. I haven't. As has been demonstrated by the post in between. I even address static vs. coincidental vs. vulgar vs. dynamic magic in my previous posts. <br /> <br /> If you want everything mages do be breaking the rules, that's okay. In the terms of the game, all your mages do Vulgar magical all the time. Coincidental magic is going with the flow. It is. I would go with Dataweaver and say &quot;bending&quot; is pretty much the right way to address it. That's why it is easier and has less of a downside. <br /> <br /> BUT, that doesn't mean that you can draw the lines you're drawing for the game as whole. This is magic about this line and it's not magic below. The explicit rules, the core fluff of mage, the ponderings and musing of the creators (including and especially Brucato) don't support the distinctions you are making. Which is FINE. It's your game and you can do it however you want. I'm not even sure how having it work your way would make a material difference on the table in pretty much every Mage game I've ever participated in. (Most games I've been involved in have significant plot happening over armchair philosophizing about the nature of &quot;what&quot; and &quot;is&quot; and variegies of &quot;not&quot;. Mages seem to be more like action-oriented practical application philosophers...) <br /> <br /> Concepts like &quot;Consensus&quot;, &quot;Coincidental&quot;, &quot;Static&quot;, &quot;Vulgar&quot;, &quot;Dynamic&quot;, etc. don't just imply a continuum, they rely on it. And it's a continuum of magic, not &quot;not-magic vs. magic&quot;. Magic, for these purposes doesn't follow the Consensus definition, which is all about supernatural agency. All conscious agency to alter the self or environment by sentient beings with Avatars is magic. If anything, the &quot;not magic vs. magic&quot; line is much lower... if something without an Avatar does it, then it's &quot;not magic&quot;....<br /> <br /> But even that falls flat when other splats are brought into play, because that makes vampires, werewolves, et al. make sense. Maybe it's good enough to have an &quot;Avatar shaped hole&quot; for vampires? I dunno.... Maybe it's more that the other splats are evincing powers from being acted upon as opposed to being the source of their own agency? Maybe they predate the Consensus and are running off a different system that still works for them? (Previous iterations of the Matrix...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:00:10-08:00","id":1011122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011084#post1011084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I never really understood the Metaphysics any differently than what M20 states, even in the Revised book era.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the Revised book even describes the 'static effects' of Coincidental Magick as a mere 'mimicry', and the pre-Revised corebooks also state what M20 states...so, in a way, the sweeping change in wording of what the difference between Static and True/Dynamic magic is, was made by Revised <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And in the end didn't make a difference, anyways)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Revised making a big change relative to the previous edition is much more likely. I just thought that in such a case M20 would say &quot;you have options 2 and 3 to choose from&quot; on the matter, since it was said that it presents the GM a choice in cases where setting elements are different between editions.<br /> <br /> (I'm currently playing Revised, and it's been a long time since my previous MtA campaign, and I don't remember whether it was 2e or Revised, but either way it makes it much easier for me to recall the Revised state of affairs than any other one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:49:53-08:00","id":1011157,"title":"","content":"That's very much in line with the 2e\u2192Rev changes that I'm familiar with. For instance, Rev changed the definition of Awakening so that a gradual Awakening would be possible, instead of every Awakening having a clearly defined moment of epiphany as is the case in every other edition. It took pains to muddy the waters when it came to the distinction between mages and sorcerers, making a point that characters in the game usually can't tell the difference. <br /> <br /> That said, it did not eliminate the difference. Despite most of its efforts, there's still a line separating Linear Magic and Sphere Magic (terms that are also unique to MRev); and that line has to do with the Avatar.<br /> <br /> And yes, this means that there are supernatural things that aren't magick; at least, that's the simplest explanation for the other Night Folk, albeit one that sticks in the craw of those mages who think that magick is the be-all and end-all of everything. Sure, you can occasionally draw parallels \u2014 a particularly strong one is how the Dreaming and its inhabitants are so vulnerable to human belief \u2014 but even when you can, there's always an equally simple or simpler explanation that doesn't involve the ability to bend or break reality. The fae are connected to belief because the Dreaming is connected to dreams; and anything that messes with that connection hurts the Fae. Indeed, some of the most potent enemies of the Fae are those humans who are <i>least</i> likely to Awaken. So even though Fae Glamour incorporates one of the elements of Mage Focus \u2014 namely, Belief \u2014 it is still not Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:44:25-08:00","id":1011199,"title":"","content":"Some would say that static magick and supernatural exist because humanity believes in them, in one way or another: Vampires and Garou are part of local folklores, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:59:09-08:00","id":1011209,"title":"","content":"When you have Bygones and Fae as examples of supernaturals who are clearly affected by human belief (or rather, by human disbelief), the argument that vampires and werewolves subsist on human belief feels weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:37:52-08:00","id":1011252,"title":"","content":"It is weak indeed ^^<br /> In a way, it's like Paradox. They will say that it is because Mages use True Magick but in the end... it's mostly to balance the game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T22:00:51-08:00","id":1011851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1006919-sphere-limits?p=1011209#post1011209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have Bygones and Fae as examples of supernaturals who are clearly affected by human belief (or rather, by human disbelief), the argument that vampires and werewolves subsist on human belief feels weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Subsist&quot; is a loaded word here. More like, they exist in the first place because of human belief, but since then have taken on a life of their own.<br /> <br /> Moreover, we need to remember that, as far as we know, humans aren't the only ones who determine the Consensus. Spirits might contribute to it too, as can the supernaturals themselves, and even gods. The Almighty who cursed Caine probably has a heavy hand in keeping Vampires around, and Gaia does the same for Werewolves.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I always liked the idea that Vampires and Werewolves represent a response to humanity's primal fear of unknown predators in the night. That so long as man fears the dark, these creatures will have a place in the Consensus reserved for them. And perhaps it's just me, but the idea of man's unconscious insecurities keeping monsters in the world doesn't feel &quot;weak&quot; to me. Like our own nature works against us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T01:56:59-08:00","id":1011910,"title":"","content":"Yes, and we know now why Gehenna and Apocalypse are coming... The Twilight saga sure killed the fear of the dark... That Stephanie Meyer writer seems a very strong NWO Mage to me... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}